    /// Derived edge kinds, declaration order (62 §11.4): rebuilt on load and
    /// after every mutation batch, never serialised, never merged, never
    /// edited.
    #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash)]
    pub enum DerivedEdgeKind {
        /// Matches NextHop::Interface, or NextHop::Address against a connected Address prefix
        /// (11 §7.6).
        ResolvesVia,
        /// The selector's remote_ip is covered by a route pointing at the bound st0 unit (11 §7.6).
        SelectorCovers,
        /// Side 4's source-NAT trap (11 §7.6).
        NatOverlaps,
        /// The Batfish-shaped static compatibility check, only when both sides are modelled (11 §7.6).
        WouldNegotiate,
        /// A unit on a reth inherits the RG's failover (11 §7.6).
        SharesFate,
        /// 11 §6.4's traversal name kept, re-classed derived (19 §3.8). DECLARED PROPERTY (19 §6.4,
        /// recorded here per 62 §11): Cabled has NO inference consumer — its consumers are the
        /// diagram, the port row's peer cell and the trace surface. A future rule reading it is a
        /// two-level pass and fails the loader.
        Cabled,
        /// The warp's derived expansion (19 §5.3, §6.6). Named WarpResolvesVia because ResolvesVia
        /// is taken — the collision schema.edge.duplicate exists to catch.
        WarpResolvesVia,
        /// Asserted EntersAt/ExitsAt/AttachesTo only — never through a resolved
        /// warp; one level deep per 11 §9.5 constraint 1. Under-reports across
        /// warps and its explainer must say so (19 §5.3).
        CarriedBy,
    }

